Those Norns aren't the only Norns that appear in Norse lore.

Consider that German doesn't have past/present/future tenses the
same way English does.  Neither has simple tenses.

Urd/wyrde is that which is already in the well, the past sorta.

Verandi is the process of becoming, the eternal now, the present sorta.

Skuld/should is that which should happen if everything goes the way
it is currently going.  Not particularly the future but about as close
as you can get.  The Norse lacked clocks more accurate than a sundial
so the future was an unmeasurable mass not an arrow.

